# CQ-18 · composition-quality
#
# Question: Which Qualities are borne by the composition root itself rather than
#           by anything depicted in the scene?
# Persona:  P3 — director / creative technologist. Layout and focal point are
#           properties of the picture, not of anything in it; the notation says
#           so by hanging them on the Composition.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.5.1 (the Bearer column); §5.2; §5.5
# Form:     SELECT — one row per composition-borne Quality
# Note:     The Bearer column of §5.5.1 is guidance, not a constraint — no shape
#           ties a dimension to a bearer class — so this query asks where the
#           corpus actually puts them. The `?value` column shows both spellings
#           §5.5 permits: the Penman transpiler compiles a bareword to an IRI in
#           the document namespace, while the hand-authored Turtle writes a
#           plain literal, and the two rows for one scene state the same thing.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?dimension ?value
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?scene   a vso:Composition ; vso:hasQuality ?quality .
    ?quality vso:dimension ?dimension ; vso:value ?value .
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?dimension
